WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.160
Hello, Office Ladies listeners.
各位《办公室女士》的听众朋友们，大家好。

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.000
How are you doing?
你们好吗？

3
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.700
We hope you're doing great this holiday season, and we have something fun for you today.
希望大家在这个节日季过得愉快，今天我们为大家准备了一些有趣的内容。

4
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:18.000
We thought we would rerun our Star Wars Holiday Special Movie Breakdown for you.
我们想重播一下《星球大战假日特辑》的电影解析节目。

5
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:23.020
This movie, if you haven't seen it, oh my God, it is spectacular in so many ways.
如果你还没看过这部电影，天哪，它在很多方面都堪称壮观。

6
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.400
But, you know, so many people have traditions of watching their favorite
但你知道，很多人每年都有观看自己最喜爱的

7
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.960
holiday movies or holiday TV episodes every year.
节日电影或节日电视节目的传统。

8
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.340
And a few of you said this would be on your wish list,
你们中有几位说这会在你们的愿望清单上，

9
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.140
that we play this every year.
希望我们每年都播一次。

10
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.460
And so we're going to do that.
所以我们决定这么做。

11
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.040
Yes.
没错。

12
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.120
If you need something to listen to
如果你需要一些东西来打发时间，

13
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.520
while you're doing your last minute holiday shopping
比如在你做最后一刻的节日购物时，

14
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.120
or holiday wrapping, we want to keep you company.
或者在包装节日礼物时，我们想陪伴着你。

15
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:47.840
So we're sort of doing that thing
所以我们就像是做了一件

16
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.540
where we move something to the top of your email inbox.
把某样东西置顶到你收件箱顶部的事情。

17
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.080
You don't have to search for it.
你不需要去搜索它。

18
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.600
We're putting it right here for you.
我们直接把它放在这里给你。

19
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:53.920
Yeah.
是的。

20
00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.540
So happy Friday, happy holidays.
祝大家周五快乐，节日快乐。

21
00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.980
And here is our Star Wars Holiday Special.
这就是我们的《星球大战假日特辑》节目。

22
00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:05.370
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

23
00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.770
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

24
00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.330
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

25
00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:09.590
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

26
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:13.750
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在我们专门为你们制作了终极的《办公室》粉丝播客。

27
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:18.250
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访、幕后细节和许多闺蜜故事，深入探索《办公室》的世界。

28
00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:21.410
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0版。

29
00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.470
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
你好。

30
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:26.840
Hello.
你好。

31
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.040
Well, hello to you.
嗯，你好。

32
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.940
You guys, we showed up today.
伙计们，我们今天很有默契。

33
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.400
We had not spoken to one another this morning.
我们今天早上还没通过话。

34
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.640
We are both in black and white striped sweater things.
我们俩都穿了黑白条纹的毛衣。

35
00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.880
We just look at us.
快看看我们。

36
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.240
We dressed almost the same today.
我们今天穿得几乎一模一样。

37
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.260
Should we talk about what we're doing today?
我们要聊聊今天要做什么吗？

38
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:45.960
Yes.
好的。

39
00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:51.840
Well, you know, everyone, from time to time, we are going to be dipping into our Dear Office
嗯，大家知道，我们时不时会翻阅我们的“亲爱的办公室女士”信箱，

40
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.700
Ladies mailbag and doing episodes based on your suggestions.
并根据你们的建议制作节目。

41
00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.200
Yeah, you heard us right.
没错，你们没听错。

42
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.640
Your suggestions will become an episode.
你们的建议将成为一期节目。

43
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:09.140
These episode suggestions can be office-related or not office-related, which brings us to today.
这些节目建议可以与《办公室》有关，也可以无关，这正是我们今天的主题。

44
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.560
To kick things off, we had our very own Cassie Jerkins make the first recommendation.
为了开个好头，我们请我们的凯西·杰金斯提出了第一个建议。

45
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.280
Cassie, would you like to share with everyone what you wanted us to do an episode about?
凯西，你想和大家分享一下你希望我们做哪一期的节目吗？

46
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:28.800
So I was in the office ladies' mailbag, and a lot of people were requesting Star Wars or like a fantasy movie breakdown.
我在翻看《办公室女士》的信箱时，很多人都在要求解析《星球大战》或者类似的奇幻电影。

47
00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:29.360
Yeah!
没错！

48
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.140
So I was thinking, like, okay, it's the start of December.
所以我在想，好吧，现在是十二月初了。

49
00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.060
It's the holiday season.
正是节日季。

50
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:44.340
So I think you all should break down one of the strangest things in the Star Wars universe, the Star Wars Holiday Special.
所以我认为你们应该解析一下《星球大战》宇宙中最奇怪的东西之一，《星球大战假日特辑》。

51
00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.740
Holy crapsticks.
我的天呐。

52
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.940
Where do we begin?
我们从哪儿说起呢？

53
00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.480
I mean, I had never seen this before.
我是说，我以前从没见过这东西。

54
00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.440
I'd never heard of it.
我听都没听说过。

55
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.140
I just watched Star Wars for the first time last year.
我去年才第一次看《星球大战》。

56
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.040
I had never seen it either.
我也没看过。

57
00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.800
I had heard not so great things.
我听说评价不怎么样。

58
00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:07.460
When we were recording our second drink for this week, Sam insisted that it was, quote-unquote, great.
当我们录制本周第二杯饮品时，Sam坚持说它“非常棒”。

59
00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:08.440
Sam?
Sam？

60
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:09.320
It is.
确实很棒。

61
00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.360
It is really great.
真的非常棒。

62
00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:18.700
You know, we had to ask Ainsley to do an outline of this for us, and we felt like she needed to be here because, Ainsley, what do you have to say?
你知道，我们不得不请Ainsley帮我们写个大纲，我们觉得她得亲自到场，因为，Ainsley，你有什么想说的吗？

63
00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.080
Well, I thought I was on drugs while I was watching it.
嗯，看的时候我以为自己嗑药了。

64
00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.280
I wasn't.
其实我没嗑。

65
00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:29.340
Ainsley, when we got your outline and we started reading it, it was so funny.
Ainsley，当我们拿到你的大纲开始读的时候，真的太搞笑了。

66
00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:32.440
You were clearly so like, what the hell is this?
你当时显然是一脸“这到底是什么鬼”的表情。

67
00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.520
Well, should we get into it, lady?
好了，我们要开始了吗，女士们？

68
00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:37.320
We better.
最好是这样。

69
00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.940
Here it is, the Star Wars Holiday Special 1978.
这就是《星球大战假日特辑》，1978年版。

70
00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.480
This was a story by George Lucas.
故事由乔治·卢卡斯构思。

71
00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.880
It was written by Bruce Falanche, Rod Warren, Pat Prophet, and Leonard Ripps,
编剧是Bruce Falanche、Rod Warren、Pat Prophet和Leonard Ripps，

72
00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:56.600
with original songs by Mitzi and Kenny Welch, and costumes by Bob Mackie.
原创歌曲由Mitzi和Kenny Welch创作，服装由Bob Mackie设计。

73
00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:57.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

74
00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.260
Fast Fact No.
速览事实第一条。

75
00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.300
1 is titled, What Is This?
标题是：这到底是什么？

76
00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:07.120
I don't know what it is.
我不知道这是什么。

77
00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.300
I don't know.
我不知道。

78
00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:18.380
The Star Wars Holiday Special was a television special originally broadcast by CBS on November 17, 1978.
《星球大战假日特辑》是一部电视特辑，最初于1978年11月17日在CBS播出。

79
00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.060
That was the weekend before Thanksgiving.
那是感恩节前的那个周末。

80
00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.060
This was prime placement.
这可是黄金档期。

81
00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.240
Star Wars the movie had been released the year prior.
《星球大战》电影在前一年上映。

82
00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:33.400
and had become the highest grossing movie in history, as well as a cultural phenomenon.
并成为了史上票房最高的电影，也是一种文化现象。

83
00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:38.960
The sequel, The Empire Strikes Back, was still two years away.
续集《帝国反击战》还要两年才会上映。

84
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:51.360
So George Lucas was convinced by people to do this Star Wars holiday television special
所以乔治·卢卡斯被说服制作了这个《星球大战》假日电视特辑，

85
00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.560
as a way of keeping fans interested in the franchise.
以此来保持粉丝对该系列的兴趣。

86
00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.420
Yes, he has been quoted many times saying that he got talked into this.
没错，他多次公开表示自己是被说服才做这个的。

87
00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.220
He wants you to know.
他想让大家都知道这一点。

88
00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:00.600
Yeah.
是啊。

89
00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:05.000
But they said we could sell more toys this holiday season.
但他们说这样能在这个假日季多卖点玩具。

90
00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.820
And maybe this was one of their pitches.
也许这就是他们的推销话术之一。

91
00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:13.480
Maybe we could make some new fans who didn't see Star Wars in theaters.
也许我们可以借此吸引那些没在电影院看过《星球大战》的新粉丝。

92
00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.100
Yeah.
是啊。

93
00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.880
There's like three of them left.
大概还剩三个人没看过吧。

94
00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.100
Maybe they'll get on board.
也许他们会入坑。

95
00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:22.160
Everyone had seen this movie at this time, except for you.
当时每个人都看过这部电影，除了你。

96
00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.040
Except for me.
除了我。

97
00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.140
This was for you, Jenna.
这是为你准备的，Jenna。

98
00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.580
This holiday special was for you.
这个假日特辑就是为你拍的。

99
00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:28.380
Oh, boy.
天哪。

100
00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.960
Well, wow.
哇哦。

101
00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:37.360
This movie special stars the main cast of the original Star Wars.
这部特别节目由《星球大战》原班人马主演。

102
00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.460
Everyone has a cameo.
每个人都有客串。

103
00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:39.940
Yes.
没错。

104
00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:45.620
And like traditional holiday specials of the time, it is a type of variety show.
而且就像当时传统的节日特别节目一样，它是一种综艺秀。

105
00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:49.060
So it has cameos by comedic actors.
所以里面有喜剧演员客串。

106
00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.100
It has musical numbers.
还有音乐表演。

107
00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:56.240
Angela, take us back to 1978 when this special aired.
安吉拉，带我们回到1978年这档节目播出的那个时候吧。

108
00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:59.500
You said you wanted to talk a little bit about it.
你说过你想聊聊它。

109
00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.140
Yeah, I just wanted to get you in the mood for 1978.
是啊，我只是想让你感受一下1978年的氛围。

110
00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:02.760
Okay.
好的。

111
00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:09.760
First of all, the best-selling album of 1978 was Saturday Night Fever, the soundtrack by the Bee Gees.
首先，1978年最畅销的专辑是《周末狂热夜》，也就是比吉斯乐队制作的原声带。

112
00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.680
It spent 24 weeks at number one on the Billboard 200.
它在公告牌二百强专辑榜上蝉联了24周冠军。

113
00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:14.980
24 weeks.
24周。

114
00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:15.940
That's a long time.
那可真是很长一段时间。

115
00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.000
I think we need to hear it to set the mood.
我想我们需要听听它来找找感觉。

116
00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:18.420
Okay.
好的。

117
00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:25.460
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

118
00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:27.840
Where are my roller skates?
我的旱冰鞋在哪儿？

119
00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:28.260
Come on.
来吧。

120
00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.200
So this is what people were grooving out to.
这就是当时人们跟着摇摆的音乐。

121
00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:31.720
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

122
00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.100
Are you feeling it?
你感觉到了吗？

123
00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.120
Are you feeling 1978?
你感受到1978年的氛围了吗？

124
00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.400
I'm feeling it.
我感觉到了。

125
00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:35.740
Yeah.
没错。

126
00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:36.700
All right.
好的。

127
00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:40.040
I can feel my landline phone in my hand right now.
我现在感觉手里正拿着座机电话。

128
00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:40.940
How happy are you?
你有多开心？

129
00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:41.780
I love it.
我喜欢这种感觉。

130
00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.140
I'm feeling my roller skates.
我感觉自己穿上了旱冰鞋。

131
00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:43.460
Okay.
好的。

132
00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.900
And you might be curious what the most popular toys were.
你可能很好奇当时最受欢迎的玩具是什么。

133
00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.760
I'm going to give you the top three.
我来告诉你前三名。

134
00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:53.860
The first one, you guessed it, were the Star Wars figurines that came out.
第一个，你猜对了，就是当时推出的《星球大战》人偶。

135
00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.200
Now, they came out in 1977.
它们是在1977年推出的。

136
00:06:56.860 --> 00:07:00.720
The toy manufacturer, Kenner, ran out of them almost immediately.
玩具制造商肯纳公司几乎立刻就卖断货了。

137
00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.740
They had to give out certificates.
他们不得不发放兑换券。

138
00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:10.460
Like you could pay $9 and you got like a piece of cardboard that you could then mail into the manufacturer.
就像你付9美元，就能得到一张硬纸板，然后你可以把它寄给制造商。

139
00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:13.880
And then they would, when they finally got back in stock, mail you a figurine.
等他们终于有货了，就会给你寄一个人偶。

140
00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:14.440
Wow.
哇。

141
00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.160
They were called the early bird figurines.
它们被称为“早鸟”人偶。

142
00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.700
They now go for thousands of dollars.
现在它们能卖到几千美元。

143
00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:30.720
For example, the 1978 Luke Skywalker Early Bird 12A figurine is a huge ticket item, but guess which one has sold for the most?
比如，1978年的卢克·天行者“早鸟”12A人偶是非常抢手的商品，但你猜哪一个卖得最贵？

144
00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:33.940
It set a world's most valuable toy record.
它创下了世界上最有价值玩具的纪录。

145
00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:41.560
I actually weirdly think I know this because I feel like Mark Hamill did an interview about it once.
我居然奇怪地觉得我知道这个，因为我记得马克·哈米尔好像曾经接受过关于它的采访。

146
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.100
Is it a Luke Skywalker something?
是卢克·天行者的什么东西吗？

147
00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:44.780
No.
不是。

148
00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:51.940
I thought there was like some batch of him that was made incorrectly, and someone has one.
我以为有一批他的人偶做错了，然后有人收藏了一个。

149
00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.560
Well, those always go for a lot, and you're on the right track here.
嗯，那些确实总是卖得很贵，你的方向是对的。

150
00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:05.840
But the extremely rare Star Wars action figure that sold for $525,000, half a million dollars, for a little figurine,
但那个极其罕见的《星球大战》可动人偶卖出了52.5万美元，半百万美元，就为了一个小人偶，

151
00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:11.600
was a hand-painted missile-firing model of the bounty hunter Boba Fett.
是一个手工涂装、可发射导弹的赏金猎人波巴·费特模型。

152
00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:12.740
Oh!
噢！

153
00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:13.200
Yeah.
是啊。

